   "gap": "ED26-METHOD-entropy-C03 requires every claimed continuous-entropy inequality to be justified with written steps. The proof of Shannon's Section 20 item 2 (annex:p15-w02b-p15-042-joint, A42 lines 183-184 and 191) abbreviates the y-side null-set step and the y-side integrability step with 'similarly', and the quasi-integrability fact (E2) (A42 lines 24-26) abbreviates its second case as 'the same argument applied to -G and -K'; these steps must be written out. The text lies in packet w02b-p15-042's files. ALSO: ED26-METHOD-entropy-C03 (extent: Shannon Section 20 in full with every proof dependency) requires item 8, the entropy change under a general change of coordinates in R^n (Shannon corrected reprint pp. 37-38), to be justified. The handbook proves it only under the hypothesis that the change-of-variables identity holds (def:p15-w02b-p15-042-coordinate-change, B42 lines 291-321), proving that hypothesis for affine maps, one-dimensional C^1 monotone maps and products; for C^1 bijections between open subsets of R^n, n>=2, the multivariable change-of-variables theorem is stated as not proved in the handbook (B42 316-321; B41 468-472).",
   "blocker": {
    "kind": "lead_owned",
    "ref": "abbreviated steps are in w02b-p15-042 files (lead_owned); the multivariable change-of-variables theorem is an exact unproved step (blocked_math)"
